  "notes": "{意味|いみ} means 'meaning' or 'significance.' It can function as a noun or as a suru verb ({意味|いみ}する = to mean).\n\nCOMMON QUESTIONS:\n- 〜は{何|なん}の{意味|いみ}ですか: What does ~ mean?\n- 〜はどういう{意味|いみ}ですか: What does ~ mean? (more natural)\n- この{言葉|ことば}の{意味|いみ}を{教|おし}えてください: Please tell me what this word means.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {意味|いみ}が{分|わ}かる: to understand the meaning\n- {意味|いみ}が{分|わ}からない: to not understand\n- {意味|いみ}がない: to be meaningless, pointless\n- {意味|いみ}がある: to have meaning, be meaningful\n- 〜という{意味|いみ}: meaning that ~\n\nVERB USAGE:\n{意味|いみ}する is more formal/written. In speech, 〜という{意味|いみ}だ is more common.\n\nRELATED:\n- {意義|いぎ}: significance, meaning (more abstract/formal)",
